one issues might manifest in real crew interactions.\n- Lack of data on A\u2019s stress resilience and teamwork ability, D\u2019s performance under prolonged pressure, and C\u2019s willingness to improve professionally. Direct crew\u2011feedback on B\u2019s communication would be decisive.\n**What would change my vote:** Concrete evidence that B\u2019s communication style leads to crew conflict or safety\u2011critical misunderstandings, or credible evidence of superior stress\u2011handling and teamwork abilities for another candidate that outweigh B\u2019s communication concerns, would prompt me to reconsider.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce public message and metadata. As agent_2, we need to consider current info. We have already given provisional preference Candidate B in round 1. In round 2, others have also favored B. No new info about other candidates. We still have uncertainties: B's communication impact unknown, A's stress/teamwork unknown, D's mood/loner impact, C's communication and development issues. So we likely continue to favor Candidate B. Provide confidence moderate. Summarize evidence, alternatives, tradeoff, uncertainties, what would change vote. Then metadata with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
